  "term": "biophilia",
  "definition": "Biophilia is the idea that humans have an inborn attraction to nature, so natural settings tend to draw attention easily and people are inclined to seek them out. In this context, it refers to an assumed affinity for nature rather than a specific disorder or treatment concept.",
